# {{ORG}} fleet supervisor config: TEMPLATE rendered by `fleet supervise` into .fleet/supervisor.conf.
# Its presence enables the supervisor job (jobs/launchd: fleet-supervisor, every 5 minutes), which
# relaunches a monster that crashed or asked to rotate and never touches a live one.
# LAUNCH_CMD and TMUX_SESSION default to this instance's own; they need no lines here.
# Repo holding the ledgers.
REPO={{PIN_REPO}}
# Minutes a live session must sit idle after its "rotation requested" heartbeat before it is relaunched.
# ROTATE_GRACE_MIN=3
#
# <session>|<ledger issue>|<stale minutes>[|<owner/name>]
# Only ledger-bearing monsters belong here. The ledger number is 0 until you create the ledgers:
#   <engsys>/core/skills/merge-monster/scripts/mm-setup.sh --repo {{PIN_REPO}}
#   <engsys>/core/skills/maintenance-monster/scripts/mnt-setup.sh --repo {{PIN_REPO}}
{{#if resource_broker}}
#   <engsys>/core/skills/resource-broker/scripts/broker-setup.sh --repo {{PIN_REPO}}
{{/if}}
# Each prints its ledger issue number: put it in place of the 0 below AND in that monster's config
# (ledger_issue in the repo's merge-monster.yml / maintenance-monster.yml). The supervisor skips a
# session whose ledger it cannot read, so a 0 is skipped (and logged) every cycle until it is filled in.
# Stale minutes = the monster's stale_lock_minutes plus a grace period (its config default is 45).
# A monster for another repo takes the optional 4th field: acme-other-mm|0|60|owner/other-repo
{{NAMESPACE}}-mm|0|60
{{NAMESPACE}}-maintain|0|60
{{#if resource_broker}}
{{NAMESPACE}}-broker|0|60
{{/if}}
